title: $:/plugins/nikorion/table/language/en-GB/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

\whitespace trim

Renders a static, read-only HTML table from a block of CSV text typed in a tiddler's body — no filter, no per-row tiddler, nothing stored. Extracted from [[Shiraz|https://github.com/kookma/TW-Shiraz]]'s `table-csv` macro (part of its `ct-*`/create-table feature) as an independent plugin, with no dependency on Shiraz itself. For an editable table backed by tiddlers, see the sibling plugin [[TW-Dynamic-Table|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Dynamic-Table]] instead.

! Usage

The CSV data lives in the same tiddler as the `<<table>>` call, wrapped in `@@.nk-table-block ... @@`:

```
@@.nk-table-block
Title,Status,Priority
Buy milk,open,high
Call Alice,done,normal
@@

<<table>>
```

! Parameters

|!Parameter |!Default |!Description |
|`tiddler` |current tiddler |title of the tiddler holding the `@@.nk-table-block ... @@` data block |
|`delimiter` |`","` |field separator; use `\t` for tab-delimited data |
|`sortType` |`"alphanumeric"` |sort comparison used when a column header is clicked — space-separated, one per column (e.g. `"alphanumeric number date"`), the last one repeats for any extra column |
|`format` |`""` |space-separated format procedure name per column (e.g. `"text number date"`) — see ''Column formats'' below; defaults to `text` for every column |
|`caption` |`""` |name of a procedure/variable rendered as the table caption |
|`class` |`""` |CSS class(es) applied to the `<table>` element |
|`header` |`"yes"` |treat the data block's first line as a header row (clickable, sortable) instead of data |
|`stateTiddler` |`"01"` |key used to store this table's current sort — set it when the same tiddler holds more than one `<<table>>` |
|`id` |`""` |suffix on the `@@.nk-table-block ... @@` marker, for picking one data block out of several in the same tiddler (`@@.nk-table-block.<id> ... @@`) |
|`dclass` |`"nk-table-block"` |CSS class used as the data-block marker itself — change it (together with `id`, or on its own) to target a specific block when several coexist |

! Column formats

Each column can be rendered through a named procedure, given in `format` as a space-separated list matched to the columns in order (short lists repeat their last entry for any remaining column):

|!Name |!Renders |
|`text` (default) |plain text |
|`code` |plain text in `<code>` |
|`transclude` |the entry treated as a tiddler title, transcluding its `title` field |
|`date` |`YYYY-0MM-0DD`, entry read as a TiddlyWiki or ISO date |
|`shortdate` |`mmm DDth, YYYY` |
|`longdate` |`DDD, MMM 0DD, YYYY` |
|`email` |`mailto:` link |
|`rate` |one star icon per `*` character in the entry |
|`checkbox` |a disabled checkbox, checked when the entry is `x`, unchecked when `-`, blank otherwise |
|`todo` |same as `checkbox` but clickable — toggles the entry between `x` and `-` in the source data block |
|`katex`, `katex-inline`, `pu`, `equation` |entry rendered as KaTeX (block, inline, physical unit, numbered equation) — requires a KaTeX plugin providing the `<$latex>` widget (none bundled here); without one these render nothing, same as in Shiraz |

Add your own by tagging a tiddler `$:/plugins/nikorion/table/procedures/nk-table-formats-<name>` (any title under that prefix) defining a `\procedure <your-format-name>()` that reads the `<<entry>>` variable — it is picked up automatically, the same way the built-in ones are.

! Styling the table (`class=`)

`class=` on `<<table>>` takes any CSS class. Table variants ship built into this plugin (no dependency), ported from Shiraz's `styles/tables.css`:

|!Class |!What it does |
|`table-hover` |highlight the row under the mouse |
|`table-hover-yellow`, `table-hover-cyan` |same, with a yellow/cyan highlight instead |
|`table-striped-row` |alternate row background colour |
|`table-striped-col` |alternate column background colour |
|`table-borderless` |remove all cell borders |
|`table-lines` |horizontal rule under each row only (combine with `table-borderless`) |
|`table-sides` |vertical rules on the far left and far right of the body rows only (combine with `table-borderless`) |
|`table-center` |center the table in its container |
|`table-caption-top` |move the caption above the table |
|`table-tight` |smaller font size |
|`table-rounded`, `table-rounded-0` … `table-rounded-5` |round the outer corners (shows where cells have a background, so combine with `thead-*` and `table-borderless`) |
|`thead-primary`, `thead-secondary`, `thead-success`, `thead-warning`, `thead-danger`, `thead-info`, `thead-dark`, `thead-light` |colour the header row |

Bootstrap-style utility classes (`w-100`, `text-center`, `border`…) come from [[Shiraz|https://github.com/kookma/TW-Shiraz]] or [[TW-Tiny-Bootstrap|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Tiny-Bootstrap]], not from this plugin.

! Compatibility

The variant classes above are the same as the ones shipped by [[TW-Dynamic-Table|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Dynamic-Table]] (which adds `tfoot-*` and footer rules): installing both loads the shared rules twice, harmlessly. No name collision with Shiraz if both are installed: Shiraz's own static-table macro is `<<table-csv>>`, this plugin's is `<<table>>`; CSS classes (`nk-table-*`), state tiddler (`$:/state/nikorion/table/…`) and procedure titles are all under this plugin's own namespace.

Not ported from Shiraz: the `nomenclature`/`mathbox`/`subscripts`/`superscripts` convenience wrappers around `table-csv` (Shiraz's `ct-apps.tid`) — niche, KaTeX-dependent, and easy to write yourself as a thin `<$transclude $variable="table" format="..." class="..."/>` wrapper if needed.

! Requirements

TiddlyWiki >= 5.3.5.
